WEBVTT

00:07.757 --> 00:10.593
Abrasions on the hand…

00:10.677 --> 00:13.638
…rib fracture… from CPR…

00:14.472 --> 00:16.099
Darn! This will never end.

00:16.182 --> 00:17.267
You scared me.

00:17.350 --> 00:19.436
Too many reports. Someone take over.

00:19.519 --> 00:20.979
I'm busy organizing files.

00:21.062 --> 00:22.522
Same, I got inspection reports.

00:22.605 --> 00:23.565
I can't either.

00:26.818 --> 00:29.654
The MEJ is different from what I imagined.

00:29.738 --> 00:30.739
Tell me about it.

00:30.822 --> 00:34.117
Makes me want to go back
to university research labs ASAP.

00:35.076 --> 00:36.369
Dr. Honda, you're finished?

00:36.453 --> 00:38.705
-With ease.
-I still have some, if you're free.

00:38.788 --> 00:39.873
I have plans tonight.

00:39.956 --> 00:40.999
Oh, a date.

00:41.082 --> 00:42.000
No.

00:42.083 --> 00:44.127
Going for drinks with an old colleague.

00:44.210 --> 00:45.253
Lucky.

00:45.336 --> 00:46.713
See you later.

00:49.382 --> 00:51.634
Shall we get to it then?

00:53.136 --> 00:54.012
Okay.

00:55.889 --> 01:00.018
…the coronary artery tissue of…

01:01.061 --> 01:02.687
Dr. Matsubara.

01:03.188 --> 01:05.190
-Can you put yourself on mute?
-What?

01:06.608 --> 01:07.859
Sorry.

01:09.652 --> 01:10.612
Welcome.

01:10.695 --> 01:11.571
Hello.

01:14.657 --> 01:15.658
Hey!

01:16.117 --> 01:17.368
Hirono.

01:17.452 --> 01:18.703
Here's your oden.

01:18.787 --> 01:20.497
Hey, do you remember?

01:21.039 --> 01:23.416
That massive pile-up on the highway.

01:23.500 --> 01:25.418
Of course, I remember.

01:25.502 --> 01:27.587
That was brutal.

01:27.670 --> 01:29.589
We saw 30 patients in one night.

01:29.672 --> 01:31.382
Pretty much just the two of us.

01:31.466 --> 01:34.552
Once you've survived a scene like that,
nothing scares you anymore.

01:34.636 --> 01:35.637
True.

01:35.720 --> 01:39.432
And then, we had a toast
in that empty lobby afterward.

01:39.516 --> 01:42.852
That canned beer
was the best in the world at that moment.

01:43.436 --> 01:45.897
Spoken like a guy
who was drinking non-alcoholic.

01:47.690 --> 01:50.693
More importantly, how's the new workplace?

01:51.277 --> 01:52.570
MEJ, is it?

01:53.822 --> 01:54.739
Yes.

01:55.532 --> 01:56.533
It's the worst.

01:56.616 --> 01:57.700
Really?

01:57.784 --> 02:00.286
The police and everyone else
find us annoying.

02:00.870 --> 02:03.039
I have no idea what my boss is thinking.

02:03.123 --> 02:04.666
He's a weirdo.

02:05.250 --> 02:07.544
I'm worked to the bone for low pay, too.

02:07.627 --> 02:08.545
I see.

02:09.212 --> 02:10.797
You've got it good.

02:10.880 --> 02:13.591
Settled in nicely as a surgeon
at Meiwa University.

02:14.175 --> 02:16.594
I should never have gone
into forensic medicine.

02:20.640 --> 02:22.016
Honda, you know--

02:22.100 --> 02:25.103
Don't start with the comforting words.

02:39.784 --> 02:42.245
-Sorry, it's work.
-Top doctors have it tough.

02:42.328 --> 02:44.581
Sorry, it's work I really can't miss.

02:44.664 --> 02:45.498
Sure.

02:45.957 --> 02:47.709
I'll make it up to you next time.

02:50.920 --> 02:51.838
You know, I--

02:51.921 --> 02:53.131
Just go.

02:53.214 --> 02:54.173
You're busy, right?

02:57.176 --> 02:59.012
Let's talk properly next time.

03:00.597 --> 03:02.181
Good luck.

03:09.606 --> 03:11.816
My head hurts.

03:11.900 --> 03:13.109
A hangover?

03:13.192 --> 03:15.028
Coming into work after partying?

03:15.111 --> 03:16.446
That's just wrong.

03:16.529 --> 03:17.614
You stink.

03:17.697 --> 03:20.533
I went home after
my friend got called into work.

03:20.617 --> 03:22.327
-An emergency patient?
-Yes.

03:22.410 --> 03:24.537
He's a surgeon at Meiwa University.

03:24.621 --> 03:26.998
He's moving up in the world. Unlike you.

03:27.081 --> 03:30.418
Dr. Honda, the toxicology report…

03:30.501 --> 03:32.086
I turned it in yesterday.

03:32.170 --> 03:35.715
There's an error in the diagnosis
of the poison, please fix it.

03:35.798 --> 03:38.801
No way, I was certain
everything was correct.

03:38.885 --> 03:42.597
No, the lethal dose of Olanzapine
was overlooked.

03:43.306 --> 03:44.265
Oh.

03:46.643 --> 03:48.228
This is Medical Examiner Japan.

03:48.311 --> 03:51.481
Someone please also
cross-reference it with past cases?

03:52.357 --> 03:53.524
Okay.

03:53.608 --> 03:56.277
There's so much to do
even without any autopsies.

03:56.361 --> 03:57.987
I wish we got paid extra.

03:59.781 --> 04:00.990
Yes.

04:03.034 --> 04:05.119
Yes, goodbye.

04:09.332 --> 04:10.500
Dr. Honda.

04:10.583 --> 04:11.668
Yeah?

04:12.502 --> 04:13.962
Where did your friend work?

04:14.587 --> 04:15.922
Meiwa University Hospital?

04:16.005 --> 04:17.382
What was that call?

04:18.716 --> 04:21.511
There's a body of a person
who died an unnatural death.

04:23.388 --> 04:24.347
What?

04:38.903 --> 04:40.280
This can't be real.

04:41.698 --> 04:43.283
He knows the victim?

04:44.158 --> 04:45.618
It seems he was his friend.

04:45.702 --> 04:47.870
They went drinking together last night.

04:47.954 --> 04:51.124
Ms. Dojima! We haven't been able
to find his smartphone.

04:51.207 --> 04:53.084
There are no surveillance cameras nearby.

04:53.167 --> 04:54.961
We don't know what happened.

04:57.422 --> 04:58.464
The cause of death

04:58.548 --> 05:01.009
was a cerebral contusion
from a strong blow to the head.

05:01.092 --> 05:05.555
Or perhaps internal organ damage
from multiple fractures.

05:05.638 --> 05:08.933
This is a condition seen
when there is a violent collision.

05:09.017 --> 05:10.435
Like a traffic accident?

05:10.518 --> 05:13.146
In that case,
there would usually be secondary injuries

05:13.229 --> 05:16.232
from being thrown onto the hood
or windshield,

05:16.316 --> 05:19.652
and tertiary ones
from hitting the road's surface.

05:20.278 --> 05:21.154
It doesn't add up.

05:21.237 --> 05:22.322
It doesn't add up.

05:22.405 --> 05:23.364
It doesn't add up.

05:23.448 --> 05:24.615
Rather than that,

05:25.199 --> 05:29.412
it looks as though he fell
from several meters above.

05:34.000 --> 05:36.210
Are you saying he fell from the sky?

05:36.294 --> 05:38.755
An example, going by the evidence I see.

05:38.838 --> 05:41.132
-Supervisor.
-Yes?

05:41.841 --> 05:45.428
Maybe the crime scene was elsewhere,
and he was moved here? Or something?

05:45.511 --> 05:48.473
There are blood droplets
directly beneath the body.

05:48.556 --> 05:49.974
It doesn't add up.

05:50.058 --> 05:51.350
In any case,

05:51.434 --> 05:54.854
he must have fallen somewhere
not too far from here.

05:54.937 --> 05:58.232
Well, even if you say it's not too far…

05:58.983 --> 06:00.818
-He really fell from the sky?
-Idiot!

06:00.902 --> 06:04.238
Don't say stupid stuff, it's annoying.

06:04.322 --> 06:05.323
Sorry.

06:05.406 --> 06:07.158
These bloodstains…

06:10.078 --> 06:11.454
What is it?

06:12.288 --> 06:14.791
Possibly from when he fell,

06:14.874 --> 06:19.045
but in that case
the amount of blood is far too small.

06:24.050 --> 06:25.551
It doesn't add up.

06:27.011 --> 06:29.097
Could we ask you a few questions?

06:31.390 --> 06:32.642
Sure.

06:32.725 --> 06:35.645
Okay. First, what was your relationship
with the victim?

06:36.938 --> 06:40.316
We were colleagues when we worked
as ER doctors.

06:41.734 --> 06:43.736
And you were with him last night?

06:43.820 --> 06:45.238
We had dinner.

06:45.321 --> 06:46.739
What time?

06:47.448 --> 06:48.699
Dr. Honda.

06:50.409 --> 06:52.954
You don't have to do the autopsy.
You can take--

06:53.037 --> 06:54.122
Bureaucrats

06:55.081 --> 06:56.457
are soft, aren't they?

07:38.374 --> 07:39.667
Let's begin.

08:00.855 --> 08:04.817
As a result of the autopsy,
the direct cause of death was indeed

08:04.901 --> 08:07.987
a cerebral contusion from a strong
impact to the back of the head.

08:08.070 --> 08:09.322
However, before that,

08:09.405 --> 08:11.616
Mr. Hirono took a heavy blow
to his lower back.

08:11.699 --> 08:14.660
I believe there is no doubt
that he fell from a height

08:14.744 --> 08:17.788
of about ten meters, landing on his back.

08:19.040 --> 08:22.710
At the moment, we have no reports
of people falling out of airplanes.

08:22.793 --> 08:23.711
Of course not.

08:23.794 --> 08:27.507
Furthermore, there were abrasions
on his right arm and left leg,

08:27.590 --> 08:30.176
as if something had rubbed
against the skin.

08:30.259 --> 08:31.594
They look like burns.

08:31.677 --> 08:34.514
I wonder. Doesn't look like
the skin is peeling either.

08:34.597 --> 08:36.516
What do you mean, they look like burns?

08:37.141 --> 08:38.726
So he did not actually fall?

08:38.809 --> 08:42.855
These injuries were not fatal,
and no doubt it was a death from falling.

08:46.025 --> 08:48.319
Something bothering me is

08:49.779 --> 08:51.906
that there is absolutely
no gas in his intestines.

08:51.989 --> 08:53.991
His rectus abdominis muscle
is expanded out.

08:54.075 --> 08:56.536
Temporary post-mortem expansion?

08:57.328 --> 08:58.246
Probably.

08:58.329 --> 08:59.747
Expansion?

08:59.830 --> 09:01.707
Is there a connection to the fall?

09:01.791 --> 09:03.584
That is also unknown.

09:03.668 --> 09:04.627
Also,

09:04.710 --> 09:07.922
in the back of his throat,
his lungs, and his hair

09:08.005 --> 09:11.175
a small amount
of a powdery substance was found.

09:11.759 --> 09:14.679
Detailed tests
are currently being carried out.

09:15.596 --> 09:18.182
So in the end, we don't know anything.

09:18.266 --> 09:19.100
That's right.

09:19.976 --> 09:21.227
Not at this point.

09:21.310 --> 09:24.397
Contact me if you find out anything.

09:24.480 --> 09:25.398
Okay.

09:25.481 --> 09:27.275
Same to you, Ms. Dojima.

09:27.358 --> 09:30.945
I will if we find a witness who saw
a guy flying in the sky.

09:37.034 --> 09:38.244
It's ridiculous.

09:38.327 --> 09:39.829
First, we'll do questioning.

09:39.912 --> 09:40.746
Yes, ma'am!

09:40.830 --> 09:42.790
Could this powder-like stuff

09:43.541 --> 09:46.210
be wood dust from these trees?

09:46.294 --> 09:48.045
He climbed a tree and fell?

09:48.129 --> 09:50.673
Could be, if we found
alcohol intoxication.

09:50.756 --> 09:51.716
Then,

09:52.508 --> 09:54.302
from the roof of this stadium?

09:54.385 --> 09:57.346
But the distance from where he was found
is eight meters.

09:57.430 --> 09:59.473
If he fell from there…

10:01.392 --> 10:03.185
He would have to do a long jump.

10:04.145 --> 10:06.272
Did he even fall on his own?

10:06.355 --> 10:07.898
Maybe he was pushed?

10:07.982 --> 10:09.650
Someone with a grudge against him?

10:09.734 --> 10:11.235
That's not possible.

10:11.319 --> 10:12.236
What?

10:13.279 --> 10:16.907
There's no way someone
would hold a grudge against Hirono.

10:18.075 --> 10:19.410
Dr. Honda, let's go.

10:19.994 --> 10:23.748
Until the appraisal results are out,
I'm going to look into Hirono's work.

10:23.831 --> 10:24.915
At the hospital?

10:24.999 --> 10:28.628
Hirono cut the drinking session short,
saying he suddenly had work,

10:28.711 --> 10:30.004
and then died.

10:30.087 --> 10:32.757
He might have been meeting someone.

10:33.466 --> 10:34.925
Come on…

10:35.009 --> 10:37.470
When looking into
the victim's surroundings,

10:37.553 --> 10:40.931
it's convenient to have someone
who knew him well with me.

10:45.394 --> 10:47.980
I'd like to ask about
an incident at Miyagawa park…

10:48.064 --> 10:50.024
Thank you for your cooperation.

10:52.902 --> 10:53.819
Sir!

10:53.903 --> 10:56.322
Are you a resident of that apartment?

10:56.405 --> 10:57.281
Yes.

10:57.365 --> 10:59.492
Could I speak with you for a moment?

11:02.787 --> 11:04.121
A collision sound?

11:04.205 --> 11:05.831
There was a terrible noise.

11:06.540 --> 11:08.209
I rushed to open the window,

11:08.751 --> 11:10.419
but I couldn't see anything.

11:11.295 --> 11:13.672
Your daughter must have been startled too.

11:15.257 --> 11:16.217
Yes.

11:16.884 --> 11:19.887
I thought maybe
there had been an accident,

11:19.970 --> 11:22.973
but then I heard the sound
of a car driving away,

11:23.057 --> 11:24.725
so it was probably nothing.

11:26.018 --> 11:27.728
A car driving away…

11:29.438 --> 11:30.356
So good.

11:36.654 --> 11:39.115
We'll re-examine if there were
any suspicious vehicles.

11:39.198 --> 11:40.199
I'll re-examine.

11:40.282 --> 11:42.576
There's no way a human
would fall from the sky.

11:42.660 --> 11:43.828
No way at all.

11:44.620 --> 11:46.580
I've talked to the surgery department.

11:47.164 --> 11:48.416
Thank you.

11:48.499 --> 11:49.875
Just a moment.

11:49.959 --> 11:50.835
Okay.

11:54.839 --> 11:57.842
I really am glad
you came along, Dr. Honda.

11:59.802 --> 12:01.053
It's Hirono.

12:01.679 --> 12:03.431
I had to come.

12:06.851 --> 12:07.852
I…

12:09.311 --> 12:11.856
think I should just be doing autopsies.

12:11.939 --> 12:13.482
I am a forensic pathologist.

12:17.361 --> 12:20.156
What kind of person was Hirono?

12:21.031 --> 12:23.534
As a friend. It's just for reference.

12:25.870 --> 12:27.163
He was a good guy.

12:28.080 --> 12:29.165
Kind.

12:29.790 --> 12:30.958
Passionate.

12:33.502 --> 12:36.046
Not the kind of person
anyone would hold a grudge against.

12:36.881 --> 12:38.174
Definitely not.

12:41.594 --> 12:45.306
However, Hirono has passed away.

12:46.724 --> 12:52.813
Perhaps there were aspects of his life
that you didn't know about, Dr. Honda.

12:52.897 --> 12:54.273
Don't you think?

12:57.485 --> 12:59.069
Sorry to keep you waiting.

12:59.153 --> 13:00.279
Thank you.

13:10.915 --> 13:13.250
He was still so young, it's such a shame.

13:13.334 --> 13:16.295
What kind of person was Dr. Hirono?

13:16.378 --> 13:17.588
Who knows?

13:17.671 --> 13:19.840
We never talked about personal things.

13:19.924 --> 13:21.800
I only remember scolding him.

13:22.593 --> 13:23.469
What?

13:25.221 --> 13:28.516
You were his supervising doctor,
right, Dr. Imabayashi?

13:28.599 --> 13:32.520
Back when he was an intern.
He did nothing but make mistakes.

13:33.103 --> 13:36.190
I don't want to speak ill of him,
now that he's no more.

13:37.233 --> 13:40.236
Were things not going well at work?

13:41.320 --> 13:42.321
Yes.

13:42.947 --> 13:44.031
Or rather…

13:46.075 --> 13:46.951
What is it?

13:47.535 --> 13:48.702
Please tell us.

13:56.669 --> 13:58.045
Look at this.

13:58.128 --> 13:59.088
RESIGNATION LETTER

13:59.171 --> 14:00.965
I got the day before he died.

14:02.841 --> 14:05.135
He said he intended
to quit being a doctor.

14:06.053 --> 14:08.973
Well, I suppose he wasn't suited for it.

14:19.775 --> 14:21.068
Have you heard

14:21.694 --> 14:22.820
from Dr. Honda?

14:24.697 --> 14:25.531
No.

14:26.448 --> 14:27.449
Oh, okay.

14:37.209 --> 14:38.669
Do you know where you are?

14:39.128 --> 14:41.088
-Please.
-Bandages.

14:41.171 --> 14:43.007
I'll take this one.

14:43.090 --> 14:44.133
Thanks.

14:44.216 --> 14:45.676
I'll put some bandages on you.

14:45.759 --> 14:47.219
One, two, three, okay.

14:52.808 --> 14:53.893
Hey.

14:53.976 --> 14:56.687
-Ta-da.
-You little…

14:59.106 --> 15:00.608
-Here, cheers.
-Cheers.

15:02.818 --> 15:04.069
That hits the spot.

15:06.488 --> 15:08.407
You really are something.

15:08.490 --> 15:09.325
What?

15:09.408 --> 15:11.368
Your suturing is so fast.

15:12.411 --> 15:13.662
I guess.

15:15.080 --> 15:18.834
I think I'm better suited
for doing research after all.

15:23.547 --> 15:25.299
I want to be a good doctor.

15:27.468 --> 15:30.804
I listen to the voices of the living.

15:31.472 --> 15:34.850
You listen to the voices of the dead.

15:38.145 --> 15:39.897
Let's both do our best.

15:41.607 --> 15:42.566
Of course.

16:01.502 --> 16:03.212
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

16:03.295 --> 16:05.464
I'm Maki,
I'm getting my car repaired here.

16:05.547 --> 16:07.716
-Police.
-What?

16:08.550 --> 16:11.637
We're investigating an incident
that happened at Miyagawa Park.

16:11.720 --> 16:13.347
Can we talk to you?

16:13.931 --> 16:14.807
Why me?

16:14.890 --> 16:17.643
We're investigating cars that were
in the area that night

16:17.726 --> 16:19.770
and have been brought in for repairs.

16:19.853 --> 16:25.109
GPS records from your company car
show you parked there for 30 minutes.

16:25.192 --> 16:26.402
No, that was--

16:26.485 --> 16:31.365
Your bumper was badly dented, wasn't it?

16:32.449 --> 16:33.492
Let's see.

16:35.244 --> 16:37.121
What did you hit?

16:37.913 --> 16:39.206
I forgot.

16:40.124 --> 16:41.834
One more thing.

16:50.634 --> 16:52.970
So what did you hit?

16:55.222 --> 16:56.682
It turns out

16:56.765 --> 17:02.021
Hirono submitted his resignation
the day before the incident.

17:02.646 --> 17:08.861
It seems he was losing confidence because
his clinical work wasn't going well.

17:08.944 --> 17:11.321
He didn't tell you anything, Dr. Honda?

17:12.656 --> 17:15.784
Well, there are things you can't say
even to friends.

17:16.660 --> 17:17.786
That's right.

17:18.287 --> 17:20.873
He probably couldn't find
the timing to tell you.

17:20.956 --> 17:21.957
I understand that.

17:24.960 --> 17:26.336
Honda, you know--

17:26.420 --> 17:29.423
Don't start with the comforting words.

17:35.054 --> 17:38.515
Well then,
let's re-verify the cause of death.

17:38.599 --> 17:40.684
What does everyone think?

17:40.768 --> 17:44.480
If he was troubled by work,
maybe suicide is possible?

17:45.064 --> 17:47.149
It doesn't look like a suicide.

17:47.232 --> 17:48.192
Right.

17:51.820 --> 17:54.114
Dr. Honda, what do you think?

17:55.282 --> 17:56.325
Um…

17:59.161 --> 18:01.538
Listen, just as an example,

18:01.622 --> 18:06.710
is it possible he fell from a large truck
or a crane by accident?

18:06.794 --> 18:08.170
That might be possible.

18:08.253 --> 18:10.380
But considering the powder residue,

18:10.464 --> 18:13.217
falling from a tree
is also a possibility, I think.

18:13.300 --> 18:15.969
What could those abrasions be?

18:16.053 --> 18:19.681
Did he get caught in something
while he fell?

18:23.185 --> 18:25.854
Yoshimoto,
when will the test results be ready?

18:25.938 --> 18:28.148
They're at the forensic lab right now.

18:28.232 --> 18:29.775
I think they'll be out by noon.

18:29.858 --> 18:31.068
Understood.

18:31.652 --> 18:33.487
Accident, suicide, homicide.

18:33.570 --> 18:35.656
All possibilities remain.

18:35.739 --> 18:39.368
Dr. Honda,
let's go and re-examine the scene.

18:40.369 --> 18:41.578
Is it fun?

18:44.373 --> 18:45.958
Shamelessly digging up facts

18:46.542 --> 18:48.794
and talking about
someone's death like that?

18:52.506 --> 18:55.968
Look, that's not
what everyone's trying to do…

18:56.051 --> 19:00.097
Performing an autopsy, giving findings,
and diligently writing up tedious reports.

19:01.515 --> 19:04.476
That's about all we can do, isn't it?

19:08.021 --> 19:09.022
Let's go.

19:12.818 --> 19:15.070
I have an autopsy report to write.

19:15.154 --> 19:16.780
Take someone else.

19:18.824 --> 19:20.367
An animal jumped out suddenly.

19:20.450 --> 19:22.619
I thought, "Crap, I hit it!"
I panicked.

19:28.500 --> 19:29.918
At the time of the incident,

19:30.002 --> 19:32.296
you were parked there
for a long time. Why?

19:32.379 --> 19:34.715
That was to wipe the blood off the car.

19:34.798 --> 19:36.508
I can't handle blood.

19:36.592 --> 19:39.553
I got a bit lightheaded,
so I was resting with the window open.

19:41.013 --> 19:42.181
Ms. Dojima.

19:43.432 --> 19:45.017
The traffic police informed us

19:45.100 --> 19:48.937
that no brake marks that would indicate
an accident occurred have been found.

19:55.652 --> 19:56.653
Pop!

19:58.864 --> 20:00.157
What are you doing?

20:00.240 --> 20:01.116
Oh, hey.

20:01.200 --> 20:03.869
I tried to contact you
but couldn't get through.

20:03.952 --> 20:05.746
Sorry, I've been busy.

20:05.829 --> 20:10.459
A doctor says a body fell from the sky,
and the crime scene is in total chaos.

20:11.627 --> 20:13.712
Please don't inform my company.

20:13.795 --> 20:14.796
Yeah, all right.

20:14.880 --> 20:16.798
Is he a person of interest?

20:16.882 --> 20:18.634
He hit an animal near the scene.

20:18.717 --> 20:21.720
Did you hear any sounds
like a collision near the scene?

20:21.803 --> 20:22.846
What?

20:22.930 --> 20:24.806
No, nothing in particular.

20:24.890 --> 20:27.059
The interrogation is over.

20:30.187 --> 20:31.688
Hey! What about the sound?

20:31.772 --> 20:32.648
What?

20:32.731 --> 20:34.775
You didn't hear a sound,

20:34.858 --> 20:36.360
but was there anything else?

20:36.443 --> 20:38.403
No, well…

20:39.029 --> 20:40.530
There was kind of a smell.

20:40.614 --> 20:41.907
What kind of smell?

20:41.990 --> 20:42.950
It was like

20:43.867 --> 20:44.993
something rotten.

21:00.884 --> 21:02.302
Why don't you take a break?

21:04.096 --> 21:05.764
Don't bother with that.

21:07.724 --> 21:10.060
Caring for my colleagues
is part of the job.

21:11.895 --> 21:13.981
A very bureaucratic way of thinking.

21:14.940 --> 21:16.233
But I'm fine.

21:24.574 --> 21:25.450
Take this.

21:27.911 --> 21:30.914
They say you need sugar
to make your brain work.

21:33.583 --> 21:35.252
You're quite the meddler.

21:38.839 --> 21:40.007
I suppose so.

21:41.466 --> 21:42.676
Oh, I get it.

21:43.719 --> 21:46.763
It would be a stain on
a bureaucrat's career if someone quit.

21:48.223 --> 21:49.099
Quit?

21:49.766 --> 21:52.060
I can't do this job anymore.

21:54.187 --> 21:55.897
This case made it clear to me.

21:57.190 --> 21:58.191
I just…

22:00.777 --> 22:02.946
can't handle this job.

22:16.877 --> 22:17.919
I also…

22:20.505 --> 22:22.966
did not intend to do this kind of work.

22:26.303 --> 22:28.305
And I'm always hating

22:29.431 --> 22:31.016
how useless I am.

22:34.311 --> 22:36.313
But maybe everyone feels that way.

22:39.524 --> 22:40.942
I wonder how

22:42.444 --> 22:44.112
Hirono felt.

22:57.084 --> 22:58.710
I never thought…

23:04.216 --> 23:06.718
I would never be able to see him again.

23:10.722 --> 23:12.224
If I had known

23:13.558 --> 23:15.018
it would be the last time…

23:17.437 --> 23:19.731
I would have said so many things.

23:35.497 --> 23:37.124
It's not over yet.

23:40.377 --> 23:42.045
You're a forensic pathologist.

23:58.728 --> 24:00.188
Hello, this is Masumi.

24:00.272 --> 24:03.358
This is Yoshimoto.
The results of the lab test are in.

24:03.441 --> 24:04.734
All right.

24:04.818 --> 24:06.194
I'll head back now--

24:11.992 --> 24:13.076
Doctor?

24:13.618 --> 24:15.036
Are you there?

24:15.120 --> 24:16.496
I'll call you back.

24:28.175 --> 24:31.344
No components
matching the powder found on the body

24:31.428 --> 24:35.515
were detected from the trees
or the stadium roof.

24:36.600 --> 24:37.809
Then, Hirono…

24:38.393 --> 24:42.606
It seems like he at least
didn't throw himself from anywhere.

24:45.525 --> 24:49.404
I'm going back to check the test results.

24:49.487 --> 24:53.992
However, a piece to solve the cause of
Hirono's death is still missing.

24:56.620 --> 24:57.996
I never found out

24:58.663 --> 25:00.165
what he was going to tell me.

25:02.292 --> 25:03.376
I'll find it.

25:07.797 --> 25:09.132
All right…

25:11.259 --> 25:13.511
Sorry, did Hirono tell you anything?

25:13.595 --> 25:15.096
Excuse me, I'm busy right now.

25:15.180 --> 25:16.306
Anything will help.

25:16.389 --> 25:18.266
No, I didn't know him well, sorry.

25:19.059 --> 25:20.894
Did anything seem different?

25:20.977 --> 25:22.812
Sorry, I really have no idea.

25:22.896 --> 25:24.606
Excuse me, may I ask you?

25:26.691 --> 25:27.984
Finally, I'm done!

25:28.068 --> 25:29.527
Me too!

25:29.611 --> 25:30.612
Finally.

25:35.742 --> 25:36.868
Shall we all do it?

25:36.952 --> 25:39.496
-Dr. Honda's work.
-Yes.

25:39.579 --> 25:41.539
I guess we have to.

25:41.623 --> 25:42.540
Okay, thank you.

25:42.624 --> 25:43.416
Sure.

25:43.500 --> 25:45.293
Can anyone talk to me?

25:45.377 --> 25:46.962
I didn't know him well, sorry.

25:47.045 --> 25:48.296
I've got work to do.

25:48.380 --> 25:49.381
But…

25:50.090 --> 25:52.342
-Please!
-I'm sorry.

25:53.635 --> 25:55.428
Are you talking about Dr. Hirono?

25:56.721 --> 25:59.182
Where did Dr. Hirono go?

25:59.266 --> 26:01.685
He hasn't fixed my tummy yet.

26:02.560 --> 26:03.395
Well…

26:04.104 --> 26:07.816
Dr. Hirono has gone somewhere far away.

26:08.692 --> 26:11.069
But he gave me a message for you.

26:11.152 --> 26:12.320
A message?

26:12.404 --> 26:13.405
Yes.

26:14.406 --> 26:18.493
He said he's made all the preparations
to fix your tummy perfectly,

26:19.244 --> 26:21.746
so you can just relax
and focus on getting better.

26:21.830 --> 26:22.831
Really?

26:23.707 --> 26:24.499
Yes.

26:25.125 --> 26:26.084
So,

26:26.876 --> 26:27.794
do your best.

26:30.297 --> 26:32.507
Did Dr. Hirono go away

26:33.800 --> 26:35.593
because he made people angry?

26:38.138 --> 26:41.057
A scary man was really angry with him.

26:42.934 --> 26:45.395
He said, "It's your fault she died."

26:53.862 --> 26:55.697
The detailed results are out.

26:55.780 --> 26:58.116
The powder detected on the body

26:58.199 --> 27:01.202
was sodium bicarbonate
containing hydrogen sulfide.

27:01.286 --> 27:05.415
There was also a testimony
about a strange smell at the scene.

27:05.915 --> 27:08.710
It must be putrefactive gas
generated by this.

27:08.793 --> 27:12.547
Could this be why the body
expanded after death?

27:12.630 --> 27:14.674
The gas escaped,

27:14.758 --> 27:16.885
making the body move
as if it were convulsing.

27:16.968 --> 27:18.261
What?

27:18.345 --> 27:20.555
Corpses can move?

27:20.638 --> 27:22.849
It's a special case of post-mortem change.

27:22.932 --> 27:26.436
It's when the body temporarily moves
due to putrefactive gases or rigor mortis.

27:26.519 --> 27:29.439
This also explains
the surrounding blood spatters.

27:29.522 --> 27:33.443
They must have gotten scattered
when he had a violent convulsion.

27:33.526 --> 27:35.445
What happened?

27:35.528 --> 27:38.740
There may still be a piece
we haven't found yet.

27:44.496 --> 27:46.748
Hello, this is Medical Examiner Japan.

27:48.124 --> 27:49.209
It's Dr. Honda.

27:49.292 --> 27:50.335
Got it.

27:53.546 --> 27:54.631
This is Masumi.

27:55.215 --> 27:57.008
I've found a clue.

27:57.092 --> 27:58.510
I think I might know

27:58.593 --> 28:01.805
what job Hirono was talking about
on the night of the incident.

28:02.889 --> 28:03.848
It was…

28:08.269 --> 28:10.688
What did he say?

28:58.153 --> 28:59.404
Dr. Masumi?

28:59.487 --> 29:01.698
The pieces may just

29:03.032 --> 29:04.534
be coming together.

29:24.429 --> 29:27.766
I would like to talk to you
about the incident that occurred

29:27.849 --> 29:29.142
at Miyagawa Park.

29:32.520 --> 29:33.980
Take a seat.

29:44.240 --> 29:45.533
Mr. Takemura.

29:47.535 --> 29:49.412
On the night of the incident,

29:49.496 --> 29:51.247
you testified that you heard

29:51.331 --> 29:54.667
a collision sound
and the sound of a car driving away.

29:54.751 --> 29:55.794
Since then,

29:56.628 --> 29:59.380
no other information has come up.

30:00.215 --> 30:02.091
Not one other person

30:02.801 --> 30:04.761
heard such sounds.

30:07.013 --> 30:08.056
So what?

30:13.853 --> 30:16.022
There were findings on Hirono's body

30:16.105 --> 30:19.484
that looked as though
he had fallen from the sky.

30:20.735 --> 30:21.694
However…

30:24.322 --> 30:28.117
that actually was not the case.

30:30.954 --> 30:33.039
The key to solving the mystery

30:33.665 --> 30:35.917
was the scars on the body.

30:36.668 --> 30:40.255
There were burn-like abrasions
on the right arm and left leg of the body.

30:41.256 --> 30:45.093
There is one hypothesis
that makes these traces possible.

30:46.761 --> 30:50.723
When a person falls in a narrow space
where movement is restricted,

30:50.807 --> 30:56.229
their limbs will rub against the walls
as they fall.

30:56.312 --> 30:57.438
In this case,

30:58.022 --> 30:59.983
near where the victim was found,

31:00.692 --> 31:01.901
in a manhole.

31:04.237 --> 31:09.325
In other words,
the victim did not fall from the sky.

31:10.285 --> 31:13.037
He fell from the ground into the deep,

31:14.122 --> 31:16.124
and died there.

31:19.127 --> 31:22.463
It's natural that no one heard a sound.

31:23.840 --> 31:26.759
The collision sound
echoed inside the manhole,

31:26.843 --> 31:29.387
and no one could hear it.

31:30.430 --> 31:33.808
In his body we detected both
hydrogen sulfide

31:33.892 --> 31:37.770
and sodium bicarbonate,
which is used to neutralize it.

31:37.854 --> 31:43.276
These matched what could be found
inside this sewer.

31:45.111 --> 31:48.531
You're a sewer worker,
aren't you, Mr. Takemura?

31:48.615 --> 31:51.826
We've obtained a warrant earlier

31:51.910 --> 31:57.582
and seized your work equipment from
the vehicle parked near your home.

31:57.665 --> 32:01.169
It's only a matter of time
before we have clear physical evidence.

32:06.174 --> 32:07.467
The person who died

32:08.426 --> 32:10.720
was a surgeon
at Meiwa University Hospital,

32:11.679 --> 32:12.972
Tomoki Hirono.

32:14.891 --> 32:16.434
You know him, don't you?

32:20.438 --> 32:21.856
Six months ago,

32:23.358 --> 32:25.610
your only family member,

32:25.693 --> 32:31.032
your daughter Yumi was transported
to the ER at Meiwa University Hospital.

32:31.658 --> 32:33.034
Yumi! Stay with me!

32:33.117 --> 32:34.827
Don't worry, we'll help you.

32:34.911 --> 32:36.579
Temperature 37.2, blood pressure--

32:36.663 --> 32:38.414
The one who first examined her

32:38.498 --> 32:41.000
was Hirono,
who was still an intern at the time.

32:42.001 --> 32:44.420
The blood tests
show no particular problems.

32:45.213 --> 32:47.256
She may have mild appendicitis,

32:47.340 --> 32:49.801
so we'll have her stay
at the hospital for observation.

32:51.010 --> 32:52.303
Thank you.

32:56.224 --> 32:57.934
But three days later,

32:58.559 --> 33:00.645
Yumi's condition suddenly worsened,

33:00.728 --> 33:02.855
and sadly, she passed away.

33:04.857 --> 33:05.858
Murderer.

33:05.942 --> 33:07.193
You killed her!

33:07.777 --> 33:09.862
Give me… Give me Yumi back!

33:09.946 --> 33:13.366
-You directed your anger at Hirono.
-Hey! Say something!

33:13.449 --> 33:14.993
For a mistake in his diagnosis.

33:15.576 --> 33:17.161
You killed her!

33:17.245 --> 33:19.497
I'm telling you to bring out that intern!

33:19.580 --> 33:20.665
Hurry up!

33:20.748 --> 33:23.126
-What are you doing? Stop.
-Hey!

33:23.668 --> 33:25.878
You went to the hospital
many times after that.

33:25.962 --> 33:27.714
That's medical malpractice, right?

33:27.797 --> 33:30.758
Continuing to claim
there had been a misdiagnosis.

33:31.843 --> 33:32.885
But…

33:35.430 --> 33:38.349
the hospital forbade Hirono
from handling it.

33:40.476 --> 33:42.478
He lost his daughter!

33:42.562 --> 33:44.731
We should apologize with sincerity.

33:44.814 --> 33:48.234
If we apologize publicly,
it means we're admitting a mistake.

33:49.902 --> 33:51.654
I should have urged more strongly

33:51.738 --> 33:55.700
for a retest of the coagulation function
of her blood after the first test.

33:56.325 --> 33:57.910
But isn't the biggest issue

33:57.994 --> 34:01.080
the mistake made in the hemostatic
procedure during surgery?

34:03.166 --> 34:05.334
You won't be able
to become a surgeon either.

34:09.756 --> 34:12.592
You were the one
who performed the initial treatment.

34:13.342 --> 34:15.803
Go ahead, if you want to
give up your future as a doctor.

34:22.185 --> 34:23.102
But

34:23.644 --> 34:25.188
Hirono didn't run away.

34:33.738 --> 34:34.781
He was…

34:35.656 --> 34:37.533
He was trying to expose the hospital

34:37.617 --> 34:42.246
for covering up the medical malpractice
they had committed.

34:44.290 --> 34:46.459
A statement written by Hirono

34:46.542 --> 34:51.005
that explained all of this
was also found in your room.

34:51.089 --> 34:54.133
Does that not mean you knew all of this?

34:56.636 --> 34:57.595
So…

34:59.222 --> 35:00.556
why did you do it?

35:03.226 --> 35:04.852
Why do that to Hirono?

35:07.772 --> 35:08.981
No.

35:11.359 --> 35:12.527
That's not it.

35:25.289 --> 35:27.416
This is Hirono
from Meiwa University Hospital.

35:28.042 --> 35:30.461
Could I talk to you directly?

35:38.511 --> 35:40.680
So now he decides to contact me?

35:40.763 --> 35:44.684
I thought he'd want to settle this
with money, and wanted to refuse.

35:44.767 --> 35:46.602
After the examination is over…

35:46.686 --> 35:48.187
But then…

35:48.271 --> 35:49.564
Let's go for a walk?

35:49.647 --> 35:50.815
-Yes!
-Yes!

35:50.898 --> 35:52.024
Yay!

35:52.108 --> 35:53.151
Nice.

35:53.234 --> 35:55.570
He's the one who killed Yumi,

35:56.154 --> 35:59.615
and yet he's pretending
to be a good doctor, acting so happy!

35:59.699 --> 36:01.951
-Can I have this?
-Sure.

36:02.034 --> 36:03.327
Really? Thanks.

36:03.411 --> 36:04.996
That's why that night…

36:10.793 --> 36:13.171
COME TO MIYAGAWA PARK AT 11:00 P.M.

36:13.254 --> 36:15.089
Sorry, it's work.

36:35.151 --> 36:36.319
Mr. Takemura,

36:36.944 --> 36:38.654
thank you for your time.

36:40.489 --> 36:41.699
No matter how much

36:42.950 --> 36:45.286
I apologize for Yumi,
I can never make amends.

36:46.078 --> 36:49.123
But that's why
I want to take responsibility--

36:49.207 --> 36:50.875
Don't give me that crap.

36:57.173 --> 36:58.841
You killed her.

37:00.676 --> 37:01.802
You…

37:02.511 --> 37:03.638
killed Yumi…

37:09.518 --> 37:11.062
-You're the one…
-I…

37:11.145 --> 37:12.480
As a doctor, I tried to--

37:12.563 --> 37:15.066
-You killed her!
-Please, listen to me!

37:15.149 --> 37:17.485
You killed her!

37:53.562 --> 37:54.855
REPORT OF INTERNAL MISCONDUCT

37:54.939 --> 37:56.440
1. THE FIRST EXAMINATION

37:56.524 --> 37:58.734
TOMOKI HIRONO

37:59.652 --> 38:01.821
By the time I found his report,

38:02.613 --> 38:03.990
it was too late.

38:29.348 --> 38:30.850
Hey. Hey!

38:47.867 --> 38:49.660
But I'm not in the wrong.

38:50.786 --> 38:53.789
His report is proof.
It was all their fault!

38:53.873 --> 38:55.458
Don't give me that!

38:57.084 --> 39:00.463
Hirono was planning to
expose the medical malpractice

39:01.213 --> 39:03.049
and quit being a doctor!

39:05.301 --> 39:07.303
He was taking responsibility.

39:07.386 --> 39:08.429
Dr. Honda.

39:13.601 --> 39:14.810
He…

39:17.271 --> 39:19.607
He was an incredible doctor.

39:19.690 --> 39:21.108
More than anyone.

39:24.403 --> 39:25.529
Why…

39:27.573 --> 39:29.867
Why did he have to have
such a horrible end?

39:41.879 --> 39:46.467
You could say that it was Hirono
who gave us the final clues

39:47.468 --> 39:48.594
to solve the case.

39:54.642 --> 39:57.061
He wiped away
the bloodstains from the murder,

39:57.144 --> 39:59.397
disposed of Hirono's smartphone,

39:59.980 --> 40:03.109
and then it should have been over,
once he hid the body.

40:06.612 --> 40:09.448
But why couldn't he do that?

40:35.433 --> 40:37.143
Post-mortem change.

40:39.353 --> 40:42.440
He glared at me
as if he had come back to life.

40:45.985 --> 40:47.319
And so,

40:48.529 --> 40:49.905
I left him there.

40:56.620 --> 40:58.122
It was for Yumi.

41:01.750 --> 41:03.711
It was all for Yumi.

41:33.741 --> 41:35.743
It's miraculous.

41:37.995 --> 41:41.540
If he had disposed of the body…

41:45.252 --> 41:47.296
the truth might never

41:49.715 --> 41:51.383
have come out.

41:58.766 --> 41:59.725
He…

42:01.227 --> 42:02.686
To the very end…

42:06.732 --> 42:09.276
he was such an amazing guy.

42:23.249 --> 42:26.460
I heard that the medical malpractice
is going to be made public.

42:26.544 --> 42:27.378
Yeah.

42:27.461 --> 42:30.589
Apparently, Ms. Kiryu negotiated for it
at the Ministry.

42:30.673 --> 42:32.675
Wow, I see.

42:32.758 --> 42:34.468
Not bad, for a bureaucrat.

42:35.427 --> 42:36.470
Here.

42:38.639 --> 42:39.723
What?

42:39.807 --> 42:41.100
You did them for us?

42:41.183 --> 42:43.769
No, I was just paying back the favor
from the other day.

42:43.852 --> 42:45.771
You could just say thank you.

42:45.854 --> 42:46.897
Well, it's fine.

42:46.981 --> 42:47.898
Thank you.

42:47.982 --> 42:48.941
Thank you.

42:49.024 --> 42:49.858
Thanks.

42:49.942 --> 42:50.985
Well,

42:51.610 --> 42:52.695
see you.

42:52.778 --> 42:54.363
-Take care.
-Bye.

42:57.366 --> 42:58.909
Oh, good morning.

42:58.993 --> 43:00.327
Good morning.

43:00.911 --> 43:02.037
Good morning.

43:06.542 --> 43:07.585
Um…

43:12.339 --> 43:13.716
Thank you.

43:49.835 --> 43:51.170
I've come to listen

43:51.795 --> 43:53.422
to what you have to say.

43:56.216 --> 43:57.843
I'm a bit late, though.

44:06.268 --> 44:07.936
TNS NEWS ONLINE

44:08.020 --> 44:09.563
4TH CASE OF WOMAN FOUND STRANGLED

44:15.653 --> 44:18.072
SHIRAMINE SERIAL FEMICIDE CASE
RESEARCH DATA

44:18.155 --> 44:20.866
Subtitle translation by: Maslin F.
